.github.com/users/etherealxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T04:30:14Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T04:30:14Z","body":"so i built and tested #.102579, it does not crash on 7 chandeliers anymore, but it does on 14 chandeliers (less than 14 is safe). The value is probably expected since that commit's region size is half the default. Though it no longer crashes on my ongoing project, and whenever it crash i could always lower the value, so that's fine for now i guess.\n\nAs a test, when i modified the `TdrDelay` value with the regedit from default (probably 2) to 5 seconds, with #.102579 it could survive 35 chandeliers (haven't tested above that).\n\nI have a suggestion though. Maybe before the denoising part the engine could make a temporary log file or something that will be removed when the baking is complete. So when the engine crashes, the next time user open the project and the engine finds the log file (indicating crash because of incomplete baking process), it will notify the user to lower the region size. The actual implementation may vary.\n\nFeel free to close if my results counts as fixed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660720446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"